# TUI-DESIGN-4 §7.3 item 2: round 3's wordmark is the idle tenant — the thing on screen for most of a session —
# and rendered OUTSIDE every boundary. With the boundary in place the mark's five rows degrade to five BLANK rows
# of the same height (§1.2 P-H3: a notice row would change the budget), the rest of the frame is untouched, and
# the run continues. JEVCODE_FAULT=render:wordmark.
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
sleep 1.2
send hi
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect \[jevcode\]
sleep 0.5
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
